[32m+[m[32m# ARC Developer Dashboard[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA production-grade developer dashboard for interacting with Arc Testnet.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Purpose[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mProvide developers with a reliable, accessible interface for monitoring Arc Testnet, managing an Arc-compatible wallet connection, inspecting recent activity, and testing RPC infrastructure.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe application uses Next.js App Router, a typed viem and wagmi blockchain layer, TanStack Query for remote-state caching, ConnectKit for wallet UX, and server-side RPC proxy routes for provider selection and credential protection.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Supported features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe planned dashboard includes wallet connection and network switching, Arc network metrics, recent transactions, RPC diagnostics, portfolio visibility, configurable refresh settings, and an About Arc section.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall project dependencies, copy `.env.example` to `.env.local`, configure the required values, and start the development server. Exact commands are added after dependencies are installed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Environment variables[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSee `.env.example` for the public Arc metadata, WalletConnect project ID, server-side RPC provider URLs, request timeout, and retry configuration.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Deployment[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe dashboard is designed for deployment to Vercel or a Node-compatible Next.js host. Production deployment requires environment validation, linting, type checking, a production build, and an Arc RPC smoke test.[m
